<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Río Salado</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1340</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Tarifa (1340), Battle of Salado · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Río Salado was fought on 30 October 1340 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarifa">Tarifa</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xi-of-castile">Alfonso XI of Castile</a> and Afonso IV of Portugal defeated the Marinid sultan Abu al-Hasan and Yusuf I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, who had crossed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> to besiege Tarifa. It was the last major attempt by a North African power to invade the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeciras">Algeciras</a> in 1344.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-rio-salado.jpg" alt="Battle of Río Salado" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_batalla_del_Salado_(1340).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
